# Cursor rules — business analyst review worksheet

Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` and `CLAUDE.md` first. These rules are mandatory.

## Architecture (four layers, dependencies point down)

- `src/domain/` — pure TypeScript types, rating mappings, formatters.
  **ZERO React, DOM, or browser API imports.** No `react`, `window`, `document`,
  `navigator`, `localStorage`, timers, `fetch` or JSX. Pure functions only.
- `src/state/` — framework-agnostic reactive store. Four slices:
  `taskCompletion`, `worldFactCorrectness`, `accountFactuality`,
  `responseExperience`. Persists to `localStorage` under `ba.review.v1`.
  `clearAll()` resets everything and opens a 5-second undo window
  (`UNDO_WINDOW_MS`, `undoClear()`). No React in this layer.
- `src/adapters/` — browser boundaries such as clipboard
  (`navigator.clipboard.writeText`); never throw at callers, return a failure
  result.
- `src/components/` — React + Tailwind + Lucide only. No business rules, no
  formatting logic, no direct storage or clipboard access.

Never import upward (domain must not import state/adapters/components).

## Mandatory shared components

- Every repeatable input (Conditions, Sources, Expected bullets, Actual bullets,
  completed tasks) uses `src/components/RemovableFieldRow.tsx`, which renders a
  right-aligned close (`×`) button with an `aria-label`. Do not write a bespoke
  delete button.
- `World Fact Correctness` and `Account Factuality` are both rendered by the
  single parameterised `src/components/JustificationBuilderView.tsx`. Never
  duplicate that JSX.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode is non-negotiable; `noImplicitAny` stays on.
- **Zero `any`.** No `as any`, no `any[]`, no `Record<string, any>`. Use
  `unknown` + type guards at boundaries.
- `Rating` is `1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5`; do not widen it to `number`.
- No `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` suppressions. `npm run typecheck` must
  pass clean.

## TDD

1. Write/extend a Vitest test in `tests/domain/` BEFORE implementing any
   `src/domain/` function; watch it fail for the right reason.
2. Implement the minimum in `src/domain/`, then refactor.
3. Add `tests/state/` coverage for store, persistence, undo expiry and undo
   cancellation.
4. Inject clocks/storage in tests; never rely on real time or real
   `localStorage`.
5. Never skip, delete or weaken a test to make the suite pass.

## Git discipline

- **Never commit directly to `main`.**
- Work on `feat/<name>` branches, one per sprint, created from up-to-date `main`.
- Before committing: `npm test` and `npm run build` must pass.
- Conventional Commits only, e.g. `feat(state): add undo for clearAll`.
- Generate `PR_SUMMARY.md` before opening a PR; reset it each sprint so it
  describes only the current branch.

## UI conventions

- Dark only: background `#0F1115`, cards `#181B20`, raised `#1F232A`, borders
  `#2A2F38`, text `#E6E8EB`, muted `#9AA3AF`, accent `#6C8CFF`.
- Optimise for a 400 px wide split-screen window: single column, `min-w-0`,
  compact spacing, `break-all` for URLs, accessible focus states.
- Icons come from `lucide-react`; do not add other icon libraries.
